            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Todd Heath, todd Heath, an auditor, alleged that Wisconsin Bell defrauded the E\u2011Rate program by overcharging schools."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Wisconsin Bell",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f1f6ead7d2d391deed0c9b7e893994a22b1b3b2ca28d2183d927e78b9854ec13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f1f6ead7d2d3-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Wisconsin Bell moved to dismiss, arguing that an E\u2011Rate reimbursement request cannot be an FCA claim because the money comes from private carriers and the government does not provide any portion of the money."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f1f6ead7d2d391deed0c9b7e893994a22b1b3b2ca28d2183d927e78b9854ec13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f1f6ead7d2d3-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Supreme Court granted certiorari to resolve the circuit split over whether E\u2011Rate reimbursement requests are FCA \u201cclaims.\u201d"
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "scotus-23-1127",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f1f6ead7d2d391deed0c9b7e893994a22b1b3b2ca28d2183d927e78b9854ec13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f1f6ead7d2d3-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that E\u2011Rate reimbursement requests satisfy the FCA claim requirement because the government provided at least a portion of the money, having transferred over $100\u202fmillion from the Treasury into the subsidy pool."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f1f6ead7d2d391deed0c9b7e893994a22b1b3b2ca28d2183d927e78b9854ec13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f1f6ead7d2d3-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh (concurring) joined the opinion, noting that the case decides a narrow statutory question regarding the scope of the False Claims Act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f1f6ead7d2d391deed0c9b7e893994a22b1b3b2ca28d2183d927e78b9854ec13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f1f6ead7d2d3-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas (concurring) raised a question about the implications of the Government\u2019s theory that the FCA applies when the government requires one private party to pay another private party."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f1f6ead7d2d391deed0c9b7e893994a22b1b3b2ca28d2183d927e78b9854ec13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f1f6ead7d2d3-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas (concurring) warned that if Heath prevails on the merits, issues about damages may emerge."
      }
    ],
